  "releaseNotes": "Google sign-in now sets the EasyReasy.Auth access-token cookie when EasyReasyAuthOptions.CookieTokenPaths is non-empty, as the built-in login endpoint does. A rejected sign-in sets no cookie, and a token too large for the cookie is logged instead of failing the sign-in. Requires EasyReasy.Auth 5.13.0. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-google-v1.2.0/EasyReasy.Auth.Google/README.md#access-token-cookie",
